course: dictionary
lesson: 3194
title: Without end
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: «Endlessly» comes from «endless», which means having no end. The ending «-ly» turns it into an adverb, a word that tells us how something happens. «The sailor is endlessly clever» tells us how clever he is.
explain: «Endlessly» has two meanings. The first is without ever stopping, for what seems forever: «The children talked endlessly about the film.» The second is very much, without any limit: «endlessly patient» means patient in a way that never runs out.
explain: To check your meaning, swap in a simpler word such as «always» or «forever». In «The road stretched endlessly», the road goes on and on, so the sentence still makes sense. Stories often use «endlessly» a little exaggerated, so the children did not literally talk without a single pause.
fact: «Endlessly» means without ever stopping or ending, or without any limit.
fact: «Endlessly» can mean for what seems forever, so stories often stretch it a little.
fact: «Endlessly patient» means so patient there is no limit to it.
fact: In the example «a man of infinite-resource-and-sagacity», the sailor is endlessly clever and full of good sense.
fact: In maths, numbers go on endlessly, and 1/3 = 0.333… is a decimal that goes on endlessly.
exercise: «The road stretched endlessly across the desert.» What does endlessly mean here? | Very quickly | Only just | *Without ever ending, on and on | Very near
exercise: «She is endlessly patient with her little brother.» What does endlessly suggest? | Quietly | *Without any limit, very patient | Often angry | Only a little bit
exercise: In maths, 1/3 = 0.333… goes on endlessly. What does this mean? | It stops after one digit | It is always zero | It is a whole number | *The digits never end, they go on forever
test: The children argued endlessly about the rules. What does endlessly mean? | Quietly | Quickly | *For what seems forever, without stopping | Once in a while
test: Which word is closest in meaning to endlessly? | Suddenly | Briefly | *Forever | Sometimes
exam: Why would a writer use «endlessly» in «the road stretched endlessly»? | To say the road was short | To say it is night | *To make us feel the road goes on without any end | To say the road is blue
